      "Giahoa Ryan, Class of 2011"
    ]
  },
  "summary": {
    "en": [
      "Giahoa Ryan Luong Thi Gia Hoa Ryan was born in Viet Nam, the oldest of twelve children. She worked for U.S. Government as Interpreter and Secretary during the Vietnam War and supervised local workers for the U.S. Government. She immigrated to United States in 1971. Her vast experience includes opening and owning The Moonlight Restaurant in Lorain as well as various other food service businesses. She is currently the Manager and Director of Sai Gon Plaza."
    ]
  },
